<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <link rel="canonical" href={site.href} />
    <link rel="icon" href={href("favicon.svg")} type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/plain" title="llms.txt" href={href("llms.txt")} />
    <link rel="sitemap" href={href("sitemap-index.xml")} />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#f8f5ef" media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#0e1116" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Agent Rewake" />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:url" content={site.href} />
    <meta property="og:image" content={image} />
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1280" />
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="640" />
    <meta property="og:image:alt" content="Agent Rewake: when your agent hits its limit, Rewake picks the thread back up. An illustration of a Zed agent thread that continues on its own after a usage limit resets." />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    {import.meta.env.GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION && <meta name="google-site-verification" content={import.meta.env.GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION} />}
    {import.meta.env.BING_SITE_VERIFICATION && <meta name="msvalidate.01" content={import.meta.env.BING_SITE_VERIFICATION} />}
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="top" id="top">
      <div class="wrap">
        <a class="brand" href={href()} aria-label="Agent Rewake, home">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true"><g fill="none" stroke="var(--rw-dawn-soft)" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M27 16a11 11 0 1 1-3.2-7.8" /><path d="M27 5v6h-6" /><path d="M16 10v6l4 2.5" /></g></svg>
          Agent Rewake
        </a>
        <nav class="nav" aria-label="Main">
          <a class="opt" href="#install">Install</a>
          <a class="opt" href="#film">Watch</a>
          <a class="opt" href="#features">Features</a>
          <a class="opt" href="#agents">Agents</a>
          <a href={href("docs/#install")}>Docs</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/codizelabs/agent-rewake">GitHub</a>
          <a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@codizelabs/agent-rewake">npm</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main id="main">
      <div class="hero">
        <div class="dawn" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="wrap grid">
          <div>
            <a class="status-pill" href={href("docs/#status")}><i aria-hidden="true"></i>Early release · v0.1 · free and open source</a>
            <h1 class="rise">{words.map((w, i) => <><span style={`--i:${i}`}>{w}</span>{" "}</>)}</h1>
            <p class="lede">
              A free, open-source add-on for your coding agents. In Zed, Claude, Codex, Gemini or any other agent picks the work back up on its own when its usage limit resets. Previews bring it to Claude Code, Codex and four more agents in the terminal.
            </p>
            <p class="install-label">Install in one line</p>
            <div class="install-cmd">
              <span class="prompt" aria-hidden="true">$</span>
              <code id="install-cmd">npx @codizelabs/agent-rewake install</code>
              <button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="install-cmd" aria-label="Copy the install command">Copy</button>
            </div>
            <p class="install-after">Pick the places it found, Zed and the coding agents on your computer, and answer once. Then do the one next step it gives for each: restart Zed, or start a new session of your agent.</p>
            <div class="ctas">
              <a class="btn primary" href={href("docs/#install")}>Get started</a>
              <a class="btn" href="#film"><span aria-hidden="true">▶</span> Watch the 1-minute intro</a>
            </div>
            <p class="note">Works in the threads and sessions you already have: there's no new agent to pick. <a href="#agents">Find your agent's guide</a>.</p>
          </div>
          <ResumeScene />
        </div>
      </div>

      <section id="film" class="film">
        <div class="wrap" data-reveal>
          <p class="kicker">In one minute</p>
          <h2>Watch a thread pick itself back up.</h2>
          <p class="sub">A coding agent stops at its limit at 3 AM. Nobody's there to type "continue". Rewake is.</p>
          <video controls preload="none" playsinline poster={href("video/rewake-intro-poster.jpg")} aria-label="Agent Rewake intro film, 68 seconds, with narration and captions">
            <source src={href("video/rewake-intro.mp4")} type="video/mp4" />
            <track kind="captions" srclang="en" label="English" src={href("video/rewake-intro.vtt")} />
            <a href={href("video/rewake-intro.mp4")}>Download the intro film (MP4)</a>
          </video>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="install" class="install">
        <div class="wrap" data-reveal>
          <p class="kicker">Install</p>
          <h2>Up and running in under a minute.</h2>
          <ol class="install-steps">
            <li>
              <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
              <h3>Run one command</h3>
              <div class="install-cmd">
                <span class="prompt" aria-hidden="true">$</span>
                <code id="install-cmd-2">npx @codizelabs/agent-rewake install</code>
                <button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="install-cmd-2" aria-label="Copy the install command">Copy</button>
              </div>
              <p>It shows what it found on your computer, Zed and each coding agent with its version, and what Rewake does in each.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
              <h3>Pick where</h3>
              <p>Tick the places you want, see every change together, and answer once. Nothing is written before that. Everything except Zed is a preview.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
              <h3>Restart that tool</h3>
              <p><b>Zed:</b> quit and reopen it, then open a thread in its Agent Panel.</p>
              <p><b>A terminal agent:</b> start a new session. Codex asks you once to trust Rewake's hooks.</p>
            </li>
          </ol>
          <p class="install-meta">For Zed's Agent Panel and six terminal agents (<a href={href("docs/#is-it-for-you")}>is it for you?</a>) · Needs Node.js 22+, plus Zed 1.22+ for Zed; each agent's minimum version is in <a href={href("docs/#outside-zed-previews")}>its guide</a> · macOS, Linux and Windows · Undo any time with <code>npx @codizelabs/agent-rewake uninstall</code></p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="problem" class="alt">
        <div class="wrap" data-reveal>
          <p class="kicker">The problem</p>
          <h2>Usage limits stop the work, often hours before you're back.</h2>
          <p class="sub">
            Coding agents run on plans with rolling limits. When one is reached mid-task, the agent stops, in an editor or in a terminal, and usually nothing picks the work back up: you have to come back after the reset and type something.
          </p>
          <div class="facts-row">
            <div class="fact">
              <q>You've hit your session limit · resets 3:45pm</q>
              <p>Claude Code also has a weekly limit, and the limits are shared between Claude and Claude Code.</p>
              <cite><a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/errors">Claude Code docs, errors</a> · <a href="https://support.claude.com/en/articles/11145838-using-claude-code-with-your-pro-or-max-plan">Claude Help Center</a></cite>
            </div>
            <div class="fact">
              <q>Five-hour periods</q>
              <p>Codex plans are measured per five-hour period, and weekly limits may also apply.</p>
              <cite><a href="https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/pricing">OpenAI Codex pricing</a></cite>
            </div>
            <div class="fact">
              <q>1,500 requests per day</q>
              <p>Gemini CLI's quota on Google AI Pro is counted per day: 1,500 requests (2,000 on AI Ultra). Free accounts moved to Antigravity CLI in June 2026.</p>
              <cite><a href="https://geminicli.com/docs/resources/quota-and-pricing/">Gemini CLI quotas</a></cite>
            </div>
          </div>
          <blockquote class="voice">
            "When working with agents, hitting quota limits breaks the flow at the worst moment."
            <footer>A Zed user proposing scheduled prompts, <a href="https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/discussions/54221">Zed discussion #54221</a>, 18 April 2026</footer>
          </blockquote>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="features">
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="feature">
            <div class="text" data-reveal>
              <p class="kicker">Resume after a usage limit</p>
              <h2>Your session continues as soon as the limit resets.</h2>
              <p>When the agent stops at its limit, Rewake offers to continue. In Zed, the thread asks once, with your resume message ready to edit. Claude Code asks once in the session. In Codex, you type <code>rewake</code>. A closed Copilot CLI, Gemini CLI, Grok Build or Antigravity CLI session continues with <code>agent-rewake continue</code>. Then come back to work that kept going.</p>
              <ul>
                <li><strong>Automatic, if you want:</strong> say so once, and Rewake continues without asking when the reset is within a day.</li>
                <li><strong>Follows the agent:</strong> if it's still limited, Rewake waits for the new reset time.</li>
                <li><strong>Careful with your account:</strong> credit and billing limits are never resumed, and an automatic resume more than a day away is confirmed with you first.</li>
              </ul>
              <p><a href={href("docs/#resume-after-a-usage-limit")}>How resuming works</a></p>
            </div>
            <div data-reveal><AfterResumeScene /></div>
          </div>

          <div class="feature flip">
            <div class="text" data-reveal>
              <p class="kicker">Automatic resume</p>
              <h2>Set it once, for every new thread.</h2>
              <p>In Zed, one question covers automatic resume for new threads, including whether threads that bypass permissions are resumed too. The only other setting is your time format.</p>
            </div>
            <div data-reveal><SettingsScene /></div>
          </div>

          <div class="feature">
            <div class="text" data-reveal>
              <p class="kicker">Also</p>
              <h2>Send a message later, once or on a repeat.</h2>
              <p>In Zed, pick <b>Schedule a message…</b> in the Rewake menu, type the message and pick a time. Rewake sends it into the thread as if you typed it, right after the agent's current reply if it's busy. In Claude Code, type <code>/rewake-schedule</code>.</p>
              <ul>
                <li><strong>Repeat it:</strong> hourly, on weekdays, or any cron schedule, read back in plain words before it's saved.</li>
                <li><strong>Or ask the agent:</strong> it can propose a follow-up, and nothing is scheduled until you approve.</li>
                <li><strong>See everything:</strong> one schedules page lists every message across your threads.</li>
              </ul>
              <p><a href={href("docs/#schedule-a-message")}>Schedule a message</a></p>
            </div>
            <div data-reveal><ScheduleScene /></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="how" class="alt">
        <div class="wrap" data-reveal>
          <p class="kicker">How it works</p>
          <h2>It works where your agent already runs.</h2>
          <p class="sub">Rewake gets into each place the way that place allows, and decides every resume with the same rules: it asks unless you said otherwise, asks again for a reset more than a day away, and never resumes a credit or billing limit that waiting won't fix.</p>
          {
            flows.map((f) => (
              <figure class="flow" data-reveal>
                <figcaption><h3>{f.heading}</h3><p>{f.text}</p></figcaption>
                {[false, true].map((down) => (
                  <svg class={down ? "down" : "across"} viewBox={down ? `0 0 360 ${V_H}` : "0 0 960 170"} role="img" aria-labelledby={`flow-${f.id}-${down ? "d" : "a"}`}>
                    <title id={`flow-${f.id}-${down ? "d" : "a"}`}>{f.label}</title>
                    {wires(down).map((d) => <path class="wire" d={d} marker-end={f.back ? undefined : `url(#arrow-${f.id}-${down ? "d" : "a"})`} />)}
                    {wires(down).map((d) => <path class="pulse" d={d} />)}
                    {f.back && wires(down).map((d) => <path class="pulse back" d={d} />)}
                    {!f.back && (
                      <defs>
                        <marker id={`arrow-${f.id}-${down ? "d" : "a"}`} viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                          <path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" />
                        </marker>
                      </defs>
                    )}
                    {f.nodes.map((n, i) => {
                      const b = box(i, down);
                      const cx = b.x + b.w / 2;
                      const top = b.y + (n.lines.length > 1 ? 47 : 55);
                      return (
                        <g class={n.rw ? "node rw" : "node"}>
                          <rect x={b.x} y={b.y} width={b.w} height={NODE_H} rx="16" />
                          <text x={cx} y={top} text-anchor="middle">{n.title}</text>
                          {n.lines.map((l, j) => <text class="small" x={cx} y={top + 24 + j * 20} text-anchor="middle">{l}</text>)}
                        </g>
                      );
                    })}
                  </svg>
                ))}
              </figure>
            ))
          }
          <div class="steps3">
            <div><h3>Install once</h3><p><code>npx @codizelabs/agent-rewake install</code> shows what it found, then every change, and asks once. Your agents keep their names, threads and sessions. <a href={href("docs/#install")}>The steps</a>.</p></div>
            <div><h3>Use what's there</h3><p>In Zed, the Rewake menu under the message box, or <code>/schedule in 1h Run the tests</code>. In Claude Code, <code>/rewake-schedule</code>. In Codex, type <code>rewake</code> at a limit.</p></div>
            <div><h3>Keep it running</h3><p>Zed or Claude Code stays open while a resume waits. For the other previews, only the computer needs to stay on and awake. <a href="#when">When it sends</a>.</p></div>
