      <section id="when" class="alt">
        <div class="wrap" data-reveal>
          <p class="kicker">Honest limits</p>
          <h2>When it sends, and when it can't.</h2>
          <p class="sub">Rewake has no background service. In Zed it runs inside Zed, in Claude Code inside Claude Code, and for the other previews the system's own timer starts it at the reset. This is exactly what that means.</p>
          <div class="table-wrap">
            <table class="when">
              <thead><tr><th scope="col">Situation</th><th scope="col">What happens</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr class="group"><th scope="rowgroup" colspan="2">In Zed</th></tr>
                <tr><td>Zed open, you're in another thread</td><td class="yes">Sent on time. Open the thread to see the reply.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>The agent is replying when it's due</td><td class="yes">Sent right after the reply.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>A permission prompt during a scheduled reply</td><td class="yes">It waits for you. Rewake never approves anything.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Zed closed, or the computer asleep</td><td class="no">Nothing is sent then.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Back more than 15 minutes late</td><td class="no">Not sent on its own: Rewake asks you. A repeat skips that time.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Zed restarted</td><td class="no">Open the thread once; its messages go from then on.</td></tr>
              </tbody>
              <tbody>
                <tr class="group"><th scope="rowgroup" colspan="2">Outside Zed (previews)</th></tr>
                <tr><td>Claude Code open at the reset</td><td class="yes">The same session continues.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Claude Code closed at the reset</td><td class="no">Not sent: the continue is offered when you reopen the session.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Codex closed at the reset</td><td class="yes">The thread continues when you next open it.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>A closed Copilot CLI, Gemini CLI, Grok Build or Antigravity CLI session</td><td class="yes">The system's timer continues it at the reset. Nothing of Rewake's runs until then.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>That session is open again at the reset</td><td class="no">Nothing is written into it: Rewake tells you instead.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>The computer asleep or off at the reset</td><td class="no">Nothing is sent then. More than half an hour late, Rewake tells you instead of sending.</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

